					tempSpellAction="select 1 magical effect, power or ability, or 1 divine magical effect, power or ability, magical by name on the caster and nullifies it for "+tempSpellDuration1+" min. If the spell is cast at a higher Aura than the effect or the Aura used in the spell ("+tempSpellAura+") was greater than 2 times the Title/Level of the being or creature who created the effect, power or ability then the nullification is automatic. Otherwise treat as Dispel Magic against the effect, power or ability and it becomes a contest between the Aura used in the spell and the effect where the amount of Aura put into the focus spell is compared to the amount of Aura put into Dispel Magic. Each amount is multiplied by 5% (this spell is "+tempSpellValue1+"%), and percentage dice are rolled for each. The roll which succeeds by the most wins. If the Nullify roll wins, the focus spell is dispelled, otherwise the Nullify fails. A tie result produces no effect. The modifier for permanent spells (-75%) does not apply with nullify as it is specifically designed to overcome this, albeit temporarily.";
